CP SPOOL CON START TO *

&MODE = &1
&IF .&MODE EQ .TAPE &GOTO -MODEOK
&IF .&MODE EQ .VMARC &GOTO -MODEOK
    &TYPE Syntax: &0 TAPE | VMARC
    &EXIT 1
-MODEOK

&ERROR &EXIT &RETCODE

* Extract the bREXX source
ACCESS 393 B (ERASE
&IF &MODE NE TAPE &SKIP 4
    &TYPE Mount source tape on 181 and press ENTER
    &READ VARS &X
    TAPE LOAD * * B
    &GOTO -SRC1
&IF &MODE NE VMARC &SKIP 2
    VMARC UNPK BREXXSRC VMARC A * * B (OLDDATE
    &GOTO -SRC1
-SRC1
* Move tools to T disk
COPYFILE BRXTOOLS EXEC B = = T (REPLACE OLDDATE
ERASE BRXTOOLS EXEC B
EXEC EXPLOIT (BRXTOOLS) COPYFILE &LITERAL &FN &LITERAL &FT &LITERAL &FM = = T (REPLACE OLDDATE
EXEC EXPLOIT (BRXTOOLS) ERASE &LITERAL &FN &LITERAL &FT &LITERAL &FM
* Move deployment control file to A disk
COPYFILE NEWBREXX CONTROL B = = A (REPLACE OLDDATE
ERASE NEWBREXX CONTROL B

* Extract the bREXX compiled code
ACCESS 193 E (ERASE
&IF &MODE NE TAPE &SKIP 8
    * TAPE may give RC=100 after "unload"
    &ERROR &CONTINUE
    TAPE RUN
	&ERROR &EXIT &RETCODE
    &TYPE Mount binary tape on 181 and press ENTER
    &READ VARS &X
    TAPE LOAD * * E
    &GOTO -BIN1
&IF &MODE NE VMARC &SKIP 5
    * VMARC may give RC=8 due to header cards at end of BREXXBIN
    &ERROR &CONTINUE
    VMARC UNPK BREXXBIN VMARC A * * E (OLDDATE
    &IF &RETCODE GT 8 &EXIT &RETCODE
    &GOTO -BIN1
-BIN1

&ERROR &CONTINUE
RESLIB DELETE DMSREX
&ERROR &EXIT &RETCODE
RESLIB LOAD BREXX ( NAME DMSREX

* Verify the results
&TYPE Check version in next message:
DMSREX VERSION
&STACK EXIT
&TYPE Check version in next message:
EXEC REXXTRY

RELEASE B
RELEASE E

CP SPOOL CON STOP CLOSE
